# Secrets and credentials
# Nothing under ~/.openclaw/ is inside this repo, so it cannot be committed by
# accident. These patterns guard against a copy being dropped into the checkout.
*.env
.env
config/secrets.yaml
*credentials*.json
*token*.json
*.pem
*.key
client_secret*.json

# Private development log -- contains detailed failure notes, measurements, and
# specifics that are useful precisely because they aren't sanitized. Never push.
DEVLOG.md

# Session brief -- what I'm working on right now, written for one sitting.
# Working notes, not a record: it goes stale as soon as the work lands, and
# STATUS.md is the authoritative version of anything in it worth keeping.
UPDATES.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
venv/
.venv/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Personal Claude Code permission rules -- machine-specific, not shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# Snapshot of the OpenClaw workspace brain files (scripts/backup_workspace.sh).
# Local redundancy only -- these can carry personal detail and this repo is public.
workspace/
